-- `ExistsStepSeq`/`StepSeqDecomp`/`DclExtensionCast`).

/-
  WilC5 — **vdDMM Lemma 4.2 (no new value)**, as an extension step of the §4 iteration.

  Situation (`Work.WilC5.S4Pair` of `S4Setup.lean`): `K, L ⊨ TE`, `L` is `κ`-saturated for the
  language `LEc` with `κ > |K|`, `p = (B, τ)` is a partial extension of the §4 iteration, i.e.
  `B ≤ K` is an `LRc`-substructure of the `rexp`-reduct which is `Dcl`-closed and closed under the
  definable logarithm (`S4Dom B`) and `τ : B → L` is a log-preserving `LRc`-embedding
  (`LogPreserving B ... τ`).  We are given `x ∈ K \ B` such that `x` has the *value of an element
  of* `B` (`Work.WilC5.ValueOld K hK p.dom x`: `v(x) ∈ v(B^×)`).

  Claim: there is a partial extension `q ≥ p` whose domain contains `x`.

  **The hypothesis is the source's, at the level of the definable closure** (`hvg`): *every* element
  of `Dcl (B ∪ {x})` has the value of an element of `B`, i.e. `v(F^×) = v(B^×)` for `F = B(x)`.
  It is *not* enough to ask that `v(x) ∈ v(B^×)` (`ValueOld K hK p.dom x`): even if `v(x)` is old,
  the closure can contain elements with new values — take `B` with value group `v(B^×) = 0` (e.g.
  the constants) and `x = 1 + ε` with `ε` an infinitesimal: `v(x) = 0` is old, yet
  `ε = x - 1 ∈ Dcl (B ∪ {x})` has a new value.  This is why the hypothesis is stated on the closure.

  This is vdDMM Lemma 4.2, whose proof (in their notation `F = F₀(x)`, the `T_an`-definable
  closure of `F₀ ∪ {x}`) has three ingredients:

  * **the value group does not grow**: `v(F^×) = v(F₀^×)`.  In the source this is (3.7); in this
    workspace it comes from the frozen valuation inequality `hVI : ValIneq` through
    `Work.WilC5.valIneq_span` (`valIneq_span.lean`) and its generalisation
    `Work.WilC5.SpanContain` (`SpanContain.lean`): if `v(x) ∈ v(F₀^×)` then
    `v(w) ∈ v(F₀^×)` for every `w ∈ Dcl(F₀ ∪ {x})`.  (Out of this one gets the *decomposition*
    below, and no new value classes.)

  * **the decomposition `w = z(1+ε)`**: for `0 < w ∈ F` there are `z ∈ F₀` and `ε ∈ F` with
    `v(ε) > 0` (infinitesimal) and `w = z(1+ε)`.  By the previous point `v(w) = v(z)` for some
    `z ∈ F₀`, and `Work.WilC5.decomposition_of_same_value`
    (`decomposition_of_same_value.lean`) produces `r ∈ ℝ \ {0}`, `ε` infinitesimal with
    `w = (realConst r · z) · (1+ε)`; `realConst r · z ∈ F₀` again.

  * **log-closure and log-preservation**: `log w = log z + log(1+ε)` (`Work.WilC5.logFun_mul`,
    `logFun_mul.lean`), `log z ∈ F₀ ⊆ F` (`S4Dom.log_closed`), and `log(1+ε)` is *definable in the
    `rexp`-language*: for `|2ε| ≤ 1` it is the unique `u` with `|u| ≤ 1` and
    `rexpFromExp u = 1+ε` (`Work.WilC5.logFun_one_add_rexp` and the uniqueness
    `Work.WilC5.logFun_eq_of_rexp_eq`, `logFun_one_add_rexp.lean`).  Hence `log w ∈ F`; and since
    the extension `σ'` is `LRc`-*elementary* on `F` (`F` is `Dcl`-closed, so a model of `TR` by
    `Work.WilC5.model_TR_of_dcl_closed`, and `hMCr` makes `LRc`-embeddings between models of `TR`
    elementary), it commutes with that definable function:
    `σ'(log(1+ε)) = log(1+σ'(ε))`, giving `σ'(log w) = log(σ' w)` from the log-preservation
    already known on `F₀`.

  The *extension* `σ'` itself is produced by the cut: realise the image of the cut of `x` over `B`
  in `L` (`Work.WilC5.realizes_cut`, `realizes_cut.lean`, via saturation) and extend to the
  definable closure with `Work.WilC5.CutExtendsDcl` (`CutExtendsDcl.lean`) — or directly with
  `Work.WilC5.dmm42_cut_extend` plus `Work.WilC5.ExistsEmbeddingClosurePoint` if one works with the
  substructure generated by `B ∪ {x}` and then iterates over the `Dcl`-closure.

  The result is a strictly larger partial extension, contradicting maximality in the assembly
  `S4OnePoint_general_proved.lean`; note that this lemma itself needs no maximality hypothesis.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.WilC5.S4StepDefs
import Submission.Work.WilC5.CutExtendsDcl
import Submission.Work.WilC5.SpanContain
import Submission.Work.WilC5.dmm42_cut_extend
import Submission.Work.WilC5.realizes_cut
import Submission.Work.WilC5.decomposition_of_same_value
import Submission.Work.WilC5.logFun_one_add_rexp
import Submission.Work.WilC5.logFun_eq_of_rexp_eq
import Submission.Work.WilC5.logFun_mul
import Submission.Work.WilC5.model_TR_of_dcl_closed
import Submission.Work.WilC5.dclClosed_substructure
import Submission.Work.WilC5.ExistsEmbeddingClosurePoint
import Submission.Work.WilC5.LRcSatOfLEcSat
import Submission.Work.WilC5.StepNoNewCut

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
noncomputable section
open Classical
namespace Work.WilC5

open WilkiesDesign WilkiesDesign.CG WilkiesConjecture FirstOrder Language
open scoped FirstOrder

attribute [local instance] Work.WilC5.reductStruct

/-- **vdDMM Lemma 4.2 (no new value), as an extension step.**  If `x ∉ B` has the value of an
element of `B` (`ValueOld`), then the partial extension `p = (B, τ)` of the §4 iteration extends
strictly to a pair whose domain contains `x`. -/
theorem S4StepNoNew
    (hMCr : ModelComplete TR) (hOM : OMinModels) (hVI : ValIneq)
    {K L : Type} [LEc.Structure K] [LEc.Structure L]
    (hK : K ⊨ TE) (hL : L ⊨ TE)
    (κ : Cardinal.{0}) (hκ : Cardinal.mk K < κ)
    (hsat : @IsSaturated LEc L _ κ)
    {A₀ : LRc.Substructure K} {σ₀ : @Embedding LRc ↥A₀ L _ (reductStruct L)}
    (p : S4Pair A₀ σ₀)
    {x : K} (hx : x ∉ (p.dom : Set K))
    (hvg : ∀ w : K, w ∈ Work.WilC2.Dcl ((p.dom : Set K) ∪ {x}) →
      ∃ b : ↥p.dom, SameVal K hK (b : K) w) :
    ∃ q : S4Pair A₀ σ₀, p ≤ q ∧ ∃ b : ↥q.dom, (b : K) = x :=
  StepNoNew hMCr hOM hVI hK hL κ hκ hsat p hx hvg

end Work.WilC5
